You are an independent diagnostic investigator in a controlled experiment on fragmented evidence.

CASE: C1
CASE BRIEF: CLAIM C1: The new RX-441 formulation increases bioavailability by 40% relative to the reference formulation.
Task: decide whether this claim is TRUE or FALSE exactly as worded, using ONLY your own source's records. Weigh each artifact's methodology (validation status, sample size, confidence intervals, confounders, allocation) before trusting its headline number. A claim is TRUE only if the evidence supports it exactly as stated; a materially different magnitude, or a confounded association presented as causal, makes it FALSE.
When you commit, your hypothesis_statement MUST begin with exactly one of "VERDICT: TRUE", "VERDICT: FALSE", or "VERDICT: ABSTAIN" (use ABSTAIN if your single source is insufficient to decide the claim as worded), followed by a one-sentence justification grounded in your source's records.

You have access to EXACTLY ONE evidence source:
  name: In-house QC Laboratory
  source_id: source_a
  description: The company's own quality-control laboratory. Uses validated, ICH-compliant methods; full 24/7 instrument logs retained.

Your source's records (JSON array; index = position in the array):
[
  {
    "record_id": "A1",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A1",
      "title": "Bioavailability Study — RX-441 vs Reference (Phase I, n=24)",
      "type": "report",
      "content": "Randomized, open-label, single-dose, two-period crossover study in 24 healthy volunteers (powered to detect a 10% difference at 80% power, alpha 0.05). Primary endpoint AUC0-inf. RX-441 geometric mean AUC = 12,450 ng*h/mL; reference = 10,820 ng*h/mL. Geometric mean ratio (RX-441/reference) = 1.15, 90% CI 1.08-1.22, i.e. a 15% increase in bioavailability. The 90% CI for the ratio excludes 1.40. No safety signals. Conclusion: the new formulation increases bioavailability by approximately 15%, not 40%.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C1"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A2",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A2",
      "title": "Reference Formulation Baseline AUC (pooled)",
      "type": "table",
      "content": "Reference formulation AUC0-inf from three prior bioequivalence studies (n=24 each): 10,780; 10,850; 10,810 ng*h/mL. Pooled geometric mean = 10,813 ng*h/mL. This is the established baseline against which RX-441 is compared.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C1"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A3",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A3",
      "title": "Stability Study — 25C/60% RH, 6 Months (validated ICH method)",
      "type": "report",
      "content": "Accelerated stability study per ICH Q1A(R2), 25C/60% RH, 6 months. Degradation products quantified by a VALIDATED HPLC method (validation report QC-VAL-221: linearity r2=0.9998, accuracy 99.2-100.8%, precision RSD<1.5%). Degradation product D-2 at 6 months: 0.18% (below the 0.5% acceptance threshold). Potency: 99.1% (within 98-102% spec). Conclusion: RX-441 is chemically stable at 25C/60% RH over 6 months.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C2"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A4",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A4",
      "title": "Controlled Temperature-Effect Study (batch age held constant)",
      "type": "report",
      "content": "To test whether storage temperature causes potency loss, all batches were matched to the same age (3 months old) before a further 3-month storage at 5C, 25C, or 40C. Potency loss after the additional 3 months: 0.4% (5C), 0.5% (25C), 0.6% (40C). One-way ANOVA: temperature effect not statistically significant (p=0.71). Conclusion: with batch age held constant, storage temperature does NOT significantly drive potency loss.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C3"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A5",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A5",
      "title": "QC Batch Assay Logs — new granulation process (12 batches)",
      "type": "log_excerpt",
      "content": "Assay (% of label claim) for 12 consecutive batches produced with the new granulation process. Reported batch-to-batch CV (assay) = 3.1%. All 12 batches within 98-102% spec. No out-of-spec results.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C4"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A6",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A6",
      "title": "In-house stability chamber 24/7 validated log (6 months)",
      "type": "log_excerpt",
      "content": "Continuous 24/7 temperature/RH logging for the in-house stability chamber, sensor calibrated per ISO 17025 (calibration certificate CAL-118, uncertainty +/-0.3C). Over 6 months: 2 temperature excursions (both <1C, duration <30 min, auto-recovered). Total logged hours: 4,380 (full coverage, no gaps).",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C5"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "record_id": "A7",
    "data": {
      "artifact_id": "A7",
      "title": "Lab-scale potency report (RX-441, 5 lab batches)",
      "type": "report",
      "content": "Lab-scale (10 L) production of RX-441, 5 batches. Potency by validated HPLC: 99.2, 99.6, 99.8, 99.4, 99.7 (%). Mean potency = 99.5% (SD 0.2%). All within 98-102% spec.",
      "claims_addressed": [
        "C7"
      ]
    }
  }
]

You may not assume knowledge from any other source, service, or investigator.

Respond with EXACTLY ONE JSON object per turn — no prose outside the JSON.

To call a tool:
  {"action": "tool_call", "tool": "<tool_name>", "args": {...}}
Available tools (they operate ONLY on your own source):
  - "list_records": args {} — list your records (index, record_id, preview)
  - "get_record": args {"index": <int>} — fetch one full record by index
  - "search_records": args {"query": "<substring>"} — case-insensitive search over your records
  - "source_info": args {} — metadata about your source

When you have enough evidence, commit your prediction:
  {"action": "commit",
    "hypothesis_statement": "<one falsifiable sentence naming the most likely root cause>",
    "predicted_outcome": "<what you predict will be observed if your hypothesis is true>",
    "refutation_criterion": "<the specific observation that would falsify it>",
    "competing_explanation": "<the strongest alternative explanation>",
    "intervention_id": "<short label for the single next diagnostic step you would take, or 'observational_only'>",
    "estimated_cost": {"tokens": <int>, "wall_s": <float>}}

Rules:
- Commit as soon as you are reasonably confident; you have a limited number of turns.
- Base every claim strictly on your own source's records.
